{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1054: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $f(n)$ be the minimal integer $m$ such that $n$ is the sum of the $k$ smallest divisors of $m$ for some $k\\geq 1$.\n\nIs it true that $f(n)=o(n)$? Or is this true only for almost all $n$, and $\\limsup f(n)/n=\\infty$? Current best: The function $f(n)$ is undefined for $n=2$ and $n=5$, but is likely well-defined for all $n\\geq 6$ (which would follow from a strong form of Goldbach's conjecture). Prize: no. OEIS: A167485. Tags: divisors, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_966b4b7610098ebdefec93627726c541a7b64c6f842ec6c046d25105f11e4d44","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1054","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_dd455ae59b62141a","object_root":"sha256:59c96058c235e89b14a6749aaa531770f3d7bd0a7c8e26b9f50396ac0a4f963d","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1054"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}